[35.500143, "o", "\u001b[29A\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Provider: anthropic-vertex\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Model: claude-haiku-4-5\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Working directory: /tmp/ami-demo-vqDRDz\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Session: session-20261113-190603-694-0\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Permissions: auto-allow\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[90mTip: Type \u001b[1m/\u001b[22m to see available slash commands.\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m\u2298 Indexing skipped: no project root found\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255m > Create a self-contained Python program in this directory that generates a random 21x41 walled \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mmaze using recursive backtracking (seeded for reproducibility), then solves it with A* pathfinding \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mfrom top-left to bottom-right, and prints the maze to the terminal with walls as \u2588, open cells as \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mspaces, and the solution path marked with \u00b7 in green ANSI color. Run it and show the result. \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[KI'll create a self-contained Python program that generates a random maze, solves it with A*, and\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[Kdisplays it with the requested formatting.\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m[Checkpoint cp-1794593198552-1: /tmp/ami-demo-vqDRDz/maze_solver.py]\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u001b[38;5;167m\u25cf\u001b[39m \u001b[1m\u001b[38;5;167mfile_edit\u001b[39m\u001b[22m\u001b[2m \u00b7 \u001b[22m\u001b[38;5;243m/tmp/ami-demo-vqDRDz/maze_solver.py\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;167m-\u001b[39m file_edit /tmp/ami-demo-vqDRDz/maze_solver.py